      "apiDescription": "## Models\n\nTwo-way bindings. Bind each one with the `v-model` syntax shown next to it — do not pass the prop and listen to its `update:` event separately.\n\n```\nexport type GRadioGroupModels = {\n  /**\n   * @description binding value\n   * @default undefined\n   */\n  modelValue?: string | number | boolean; // v-model=\"...\"\n}\n```\n\n## Props\n\n```\nexport type GRadioGroupProps = {\n  /** @description whether the nesting radios are disabled */\n  disabled?: boolean;\n  /**\n   * @description native `name` attribute\n   * @default undefined\n   */\n  name?: string;\n  /**\n   * @description native `id` attribute\n   * @default undefined\n   */\n  id?: string;\n  /**\n   * @description options for building checkboxes\n   * @default []\n   */\n  options?: RadioOption[];\n  /**\n   * @description type of layout\n   * @default 'horizontal'\n   */\n  layout?: layoutType;\n  /**\n   * @description whether to trigger form validation\n   * @default true\n   */\n  validateEvent?: boolean;\n  ariaLabel?: string;\n}\n```\n\n## Events\n\n```\nexport type GRadioGroupEvents = {\n  \"update:modelValue\": [val: string | number | boolean | undefined];\n  change: [val: string | number | boolean | undefined];\n}\n```\n\n## Slots\n\nEach slot is typed with the props it passes to its content.\n\n```\nexport type GRadioGroupSlots = {\n  default: {};\n}\n```",
      "renderer": "vue3"
    }
